@startuml product-status
!include ../_theme.puml
title Listing status (Product.STATUSES)

' Derived from: products models/Product, services/ListingService#create, #updateBySeller, #editByAdmin,
' #moderate, #archive, controllers/{ProductController,AdminProductController}, services/CatalogQueryService
hide empty description

[*] --> PENDING : seller lists product
PENDING --> APPROVED : admin
PENDING --> REJECTED : admin
PENDING --> NEEDS_CHANGES : admin

APPROVED --> PENDING : seller edits name, description,\nimage, category or materials
NEEDS_CHANGES --> PENDING : seller edits anything\n(resubmission)
APPROVED --> APPROVED : seller edits price, stock,\nlocation or delivery
PENDING --> PENDING : seller edit

APPROVED --> ARCHIVED : seller removes\n(stock record deactivated)
PENDING --> ARCHIVED : seller removes
REJECTED --> ARCHIVED : seller removes
NEEDS_CHANGES --> ARCHIVED : seller removes

APPROVED : visible in the catalog, can be bought
PENDING : in the admin approval queue,\nhidden from buyers
REJECTED : final: a seller edit returns 409
ARCHIVED : soft-deleted: seller edits and views return 404

note right of PENDING
  A resubmission is audited as PRODUCT_RESUBMITTED.
  Missing fields in an edit keep their value; blank
  text and a missing value count as the same, so an
  unchanged form doesn't trigger a review.
end note

note bottom of APPROVED
  Admin content edits (PUT /api/products/admin/{id}) never change the status.
  PUT /api/products/admin/{id}/status accepts any value in STATUSES from any
  status, so an admin can also move a listing between these states directly.
end note
@enduml
